WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.644
Walk the whole labelling phase.

2
00:00:06.644 --> 00:00:17.044
d, e, f, h are 2, g is 3: every ancestor fits; i and j are 7; k and l are 8.

3
00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:23.911
On equal scores this course prefers the later ancestor in topological order, an assumption.

4
00:00:24.311 --> 00:00:30.222
In the 8 recovered clusters, one logic node can appear several times.

5
00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:35.244
b has three instances: b@b, b@d, b@e.

6
00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:40.267
So a “node → cluster” map cannot represent the result.

7
00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:47.067
Each instance needs complete inputs: from inside, or across from the root u@u.

8
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:50.044
What does replication buy?

9
00:00:50.044 --> 00:00:57.978
Without replication, exhaustive search over every capacity-legal grouping gives a best largest delay of 10.

10
00:00:57.978 --> 00:01:02.333
RW brings it to 8 with 8 extra instances.

11
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:08.067
The optimality comes from the paper and holds only within its model.

12
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:15.756
The model: a DAG, node delays, 0 inside, a fixed D between, capacity, and replication.

13
00:01:15.756 --> 00:01:22.111
Forbid replication, or also weigh area, pins or power, and it no longer applies.

14
00:01:22.111 --> 00:01:28.978
This course's tests only check consistency and legal instances; they prove nothing optimal.

15
00:01:29.378 --> 00:01:34.044
This 12-node graph comes from frames of the original film.

16
00:01:34.044 --> 00:01:39.511
The film's Δ table agrees with the reconstructed edges entry by entry.

17
00:01:39.511 --> 00:01:47.178
The tie rule is an assumption; it reproduces the original result, but awaits the author's confirmation.

18
00:01:47.178 --> 00:01:55.978
And this module's place against Lab 09 (Multilevel) in the teacher's catalogue awaits confirmation.

19
00:01:56.378 --> 00:01:58.444
Six things to keep.

20
00:02:11.444 --> 00:02:17.244
Return to the comparison on the home page to see what all eight modules do.
